Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — source-developed working scene
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-10-10
Status: Independent screenplay development under DEC-0019; refinements during production

INT. ROOM ABOVE A TYRE SHOP - THURSDAY - DAY

P06-11803 fills the screen. Zoe holds her hand away from the trackpad.

ZOE
No motives, photographs, medical details or match factors. What they knew, agreed to, did.

RCP-0193 existed before she was attached. AC019 sponsored it. D3 — KNOWING SHADOW PARTICIPANT.

ELIAS
The label isn't a verdict. Look beneath it.

A withdrawal. Nine days closed. Mac contact. Four days later reopened. Confidential handling accepted before any child match.

ZOE
They didn't say yes to me. They said yes to this.

Signed terms: ordinary adoption process not applicable; questions through sponsor, not normal channels. Four acknowledgements. Introduction, assessment, preparation, documents, transfer and support payments: Brian, joint account, one Mac advance reimbursed. Five years of continuing support payments.

ZOE
No line says price of child. It still says what they paid for.

Reports ask about attachment, early-identity questions and outside contacts. Match score 97. Visual introduction recorded, three hours before acceptance. She leaves the reasons and images closed.

INT. HELEN AND BRIAN'S KITCHEN - INTERCUT

Withheld calls. A message requests stability through the sponsor channel. Brian wants to ask Mac.

HELEN
Calling them might help whoever took her.

BRIAN
We don't know that.

HELEN
We don't know it won't.

He looks upstairs, towards Zoe's empty room. Helen puts the phone in a drawer.

INT. TYRE-SHOP ROOM - LATER

Voss's separate ledger corroborates AC019 recipient sponsorship, confidential-placement support and later recovery work. Mac is a broker into a door, not owner of the whole architecture.

Zoe looks at her notes.

ZOE
They loved me. It doesn't change what they signed. It doesn't mean they knew every false order or whose child I was.

ELIAS
No.

She disconnects the working copy herself. They leave for food.

Later she writes four questions: WHY REOPEN? WHY 97? WHAT HAPPENED IN THREE HOURS? WHAT WOULD THEY CHOOSE NOW?

She closes the notebook. Those answers can wait; the boundary of the real institution comes next.
